Package: pvstackr
Title: Bayesian Plausible-Value Analysis with One Calibrated Stacked Fit
Version: 0.2.1
Authors@R:
    person("JoonHo", "Lee", , "jlee296@ua.edu", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0006-4019-8703"))
Description: Fits survey-weighted linear regression models to assessment data
    whose outcome is given as plausible values, such as PISA, and reports the
    fixed effects. The default method fits one Bayesian model to the data
    stacked over the plausible values and calibrates its fixed-effect draws to
    a design-based target, computed with balanced repeated replication weights
    (Fay's method) and Rubin's rules for multiple imputation; the reported
    estimates, standard errors and degrees of freedom are those of the target.
    Two further methods combine one fit per plausible value, or reweight the
    stacked fit with importance weights that the user supplies.
